From 18b889b08ceff9c68f62774b0881d7cc39f2bc73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:52:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] coag: surface-area-weighted (a^2) convergence check (Part B
 1d [NEW])

Add the surface-area-weighted continuous-L1 on the number density,
  aL1 = int a^2 |n_num - n_ana| dm / int a^2 n_ana dm,  a^2 ~ m^(2/3),
the weight the chemistry actually sees (accretion, monolayer site count ~ int a^2 n).
NOT the mass-density integrand times a^2 (that would be an m^(5/3) mass*area weight);
the true surface-area weight on n=dN/dm.

Gate now requires BOTH continuous-L1 norms monotone under refinement:
  constant  mass-w 0.42>0.25>0.17>0.13 ; area-w 0.33>0.20>0.14>0.11
  additive  mass-w 0.46>0.27>0.19>0.14 ; area-w 0.34>0.22>0.16>0.14
Both PASS -> the 'over-diffused tail is chemically immaterial' claim is earned; the
area weight (m^2/3) emphasises the tail LESS than mass (m^1), so the chemistry sees
even less error than the conservation-law norm. disc-L1/L2 remain diagnostics.

Also dump figures/coag_diffusion_data/panelB_distributions.tsv (per-kernel,
per-resolution n_k at the evolved time) so future weighted re-analyses need no
NEMO re-run -- closing the gap that this check could not be done from the previously
committed TSVs. panelB.tsv gains an a2_cont_L1 column; Part B figure adds the a2 curve.
